{"event_type":"review","id":"2e5b8da9f1f5c6bbf17a17c0e494e6ea7359188ca53c4f55f8ceb0e077ac74aa","occurred_at":"2026-11-07T03:05:29Z","payload":{"artifacts":[{"location":"/home/ctaylor/.local/share/crq-backfill/artifacts/sha256/a7d65adb57f9130026e20121cd6f6e945e2e5ba67dda19684cc551c48ab8cf62","sha256":"a7d65adb57f9130026e20121cd6f6e945e2e5ba67dda19684cc551c48ab8cf62"},{"location":"/home/ctaylor/.local/share/crq-backfill/artifacts/sha256/0e45084cc4fb3fa95002b0edf4a8c963c786cc00679da08160a1e19daf652303","sha256":"0e45084cc4fb3fa95002b0edf4a8c963c786cc00679da08160a1e19daf652303"},{"kind":"git-bundle","location":"/home/ctaylor/.local/share/crq-backfill/artifacts/sha256/5037c38a88156e670861dbf7fc773b8e28661cc63bfa3057e596e22717f3d16c","sha256":"5037c38a88156e670861dbf7fc773b8e28661cc63bfa3057e596e22717f3d16c"},{"location":"/home/ctaylor/.local/share/crq-backfill/artifacts/sha256/72bcc8b1ccedea588ed8fbbd66b16d50112121190f51e3eaf8b6168ba612b73d","sha256":"72bcc8b1ccedea588ed8fbbd66b16d50112121190f51e3eaf8b6168ba612b73d"},{"location":"/home/ctaylor/.local/share/crq-backfill/artifacts/sha256/d123ea724eea4d5cd035d378e49f5e8aed0004c8f20ff9c7cd61eaeef62b8a85","sha256":"d123ea724eea4d5cd035d378e49f5e8aed0004c8f20ff9c7cd61eaeef62b8a85"}],"attempt_id":"8b4a429edabc5c5d5a2c8c4e1428febe50747095bc74d30462869ed9e5c22139:0:1","base":"744dfa041981be1ac626e9fe79ae11e15b4ced35","completion":{"errors":[],"exit_code":0,"scope_verified":true,"skipped":false,"terminal":true},"findings":[{"anchor_status":"unverified","blob":"d339e24da4ca9bb05fd61c8d7330ab4fd2d42375","body":"**Update the default tool count in the config header comment.**\n\nLine 12 says the default prompt cap allows 4 tools. The default `maxTools` is 6, so the comment is stale. The 20k-char and 1k-char values on the same line match the current defaults, so the count refers to the same budget.\n\n<details>\n<summary>📝 Suggested fix</summary>\n\n```diff\n-//   - modest prompt caps (4 tools, 20k-char system prompt, 1k-char per-tool\n+//   - modest prompt caps (6 tools, 20k-char system prompt, 1k-char per-tool\n```\n\n</details>","id":"54fcacfd5282ce8fbfef8cc5bcef735bca3157374887cd1737fe89b971c8dd92","intervals":[],"path":"src/harness/config.ts","severity":"minor","source_id":null,"status":"untriaged","title":"Update the default tool count in the config header comment."},{"anchor_status":"unverified","blob":"f31d43506d7823525b04ad36d865f2e37f9c4c9b","body":"**Update the `--fail-on-verdict` header to list both failing verdicts.**\n\nThe header says only `verdict: 'fail'` exits 1. The implementation also treats `verdict: 'regression'` as failing. `FAILING_VERDICTS` is `['fail', 'regression']`, and both the single-result path and the run-plan row path call `hasFailVerdict`. The comment should match the exit-code contract that callers see.\n\n<details>\n<summary>📝 Suggested comment fix</summary>\n\n```diff\n-// opt-in: an `ok` op result whose value is an object with `verdict: 'fail'`\n+// opt-in: an `ok` op result whose value is an object with `verdict` 'fail' or 'regression'\n```\n\n</details>","id":"cb1e0d5211794956f68cdc4e2d86f35722c6c7fef2ed2c986bdc0cb4cbd8ab89","intervals":[],"path":"src/cli/main.ts","severity":"minor","source_id":null,"status":"untriaged","title":"Update the `--fail-on-verdict` header to list both failing verdicts."},{"anchor_status":"unverified","blob":"f31d43506d7823525b04ad36d865f2e37f9c4c9b","body":"**Plan-flag numeric values can reach `RunPlanInputSchema` as strings.**\n\nFor `run-plan`, `parseRunPlanInput` copies each flag value into `normalizedFlags` without conversion. It then calls `schema.safeParse` on the record. A non-canonical numeric token that `parseFlags` leaves as a string therefore reaches `maxUsd`, and `z.number()` rejects it. The rejection path is `inputDefect`, which the file defines as the exit 2 input defect.\n\nPremises checked against the source:\n\n- `parseFlags` takes an optional `schema` (src/cli/main.ts:175-177). `flagType` returns `'value'` when no schema shape or option resolves the key (src/cli/main.ts:334-345). The no-schema branch of the number-preserving rule therefore applies, so a non-canonical token such as `0.50` stays a string.\n- `RunPlanInputSchema` declares `maxUsd: z.number().min(0).optional()` (src/cli/run-plan.ts:114). A string value fails `z.number()`.\n\nThe following was not inspected, so the decisive premise is not fully established:\n\n- The call-site flag parsing for `run-plan` and plan subcommands was not returned. Whether those paths call `parseFlags` without a schema is therefore inferred from the snippet and the `flagType` fallback, not read directly.\n- The documentation claim that plan flags retain canonical-number parsing was not inspected in the returned output.\n\nGiven the premises above, the failure follows for `run-plan`. A plan subcommand path that uses a different flag-parsing route can behave differently and was not examined.","id":"6926702d4632bda23722c2979357e14c19e17f2b82f9b4015f34c2fb57bd4b64","intervals":[],"path":"src/cli/main.ts","severity":"minor","source_id":null,"status":"untriaged","title":"Plan-flag numeric values can reach `RunPlanInputSchema` as strings."},{"anchor_status":"unverified","blob":"f31d43506d7823525b04ad36d865f2e37f9c4c9b","body":"**Gate the plan-scan narration on machine mode.**\n\n`cq --help --json` reaches the global help branch before flag parsing. The scan-failure narration on that branch still writes to stderr, which breaks the machine-mode contract.\n\n<details>\n<summary>🐛 Suggested fix</summary>\n\n```diff\n-      narrate(io, `plan registry scan failed — help lists op subcommands only: ${messageOf(err)}`);\n+      if (rawMode !== 'json') {\n+        narrate(io, `plan registry scan failed — help lists op subcommands only: ${messageOf(err)}`);\n+      }\n```\n\n</details>","id":"7730dc1cfe45ecab862cb188fd747c7b094848218a0473a2ca661866468dda63","intervals":[],"path":"src/cli/main.ts","severity":"minor","source_id":null,"status":"untriaged","title":"Gate the plan-scan narration on machine mode."}],"head":"7966d2b923093860201afed98116cb34b2c98749","head_tree":"a619b07177492e5c80d4ce45880731ec409f8b2c","input_scope":[{"blob":"684a6dda654388b0aa9e3243b6d4e7af4913f12c","intervals":[[1,157]],"path":".oxlintrc.json"},{"blob":"814f8af1c75570a527c2c44312ea44c6ed0696ba","intervals":[[10,13],[44,48],[52,58],[149,150]],"path":"docs/dd-2-usd-normalization.md"},{"blob":"07f3ae6589c7574a5f139cd93e2f476a370aba1e","intervals":[[36,36],[47,53],[59,60],[76,79],[122,123],[130,133],[149,155]],"path":"docs/dd-9-api-equivalent-budget.md"},{"blob":"a2fc65974746740982756e1b848e77d01e0b86ea","intervals":[[5,5],[8,26],[28,40],[43,48],[50,50],[52,59],[65,66]],"path":"src/cli/README.md"},{"blob":"f31d43506d7823525b04ad36d865f2e37f9c4c9b","intervals":[[16,31],[39,40],[44,49],[53,62],[64,66],[69,69],[71,75],[78,82],[87,90],[92,93],[101,101],[106,107],[109,112],[115,116],[141,160],[164,169],[175,181],[204,214],[222,227],[230,235],[244,247],[249,253],[259,260],[263,263],[295,295],[333,349],[353,353],[378,379],[389,391],[395,403],[417,420],[429,429],[438,458],[461,465],[480,493],[497,507],[517,524],[527,534],[549,549],[551,553],[555,556],[561,564],[578,578],[580,588],[593,593],[595,651],[663,670],[675,675],[679,679],[700,707],[710,717],[719,725],[727,727],[734,764],[766,773],[786,792],[801,801],[803,810],[812,812],[814,814],[817,826],[833,836],[840,851],[853,853],[856,873],[876,876]],"path":"src/cli/main.ts"},{"blob":"d339e24da4ca9bb05fd61c8d7330ab4fd2d42375","intervals":[[3,4],[9,10],[12,12],[18,22],[34,34],[41,46],[48,54],[57,63],[65,74],[76,124],[133,139],[146,154],[157,159],[170,178],[180,187],[189,195]],"path":"src/harness/config.ts"},{"blob":"0c4ba667ee21d1d9c930535f29026938b58d3838","intervals":[[2,8],[10,16],[47,47],[70,73],[120,122],[134,136]],"path":"src/ops/review/verifyReviewOutcome.ts"},{"blob":"f9b679cc0241fe502c2ba58ea4b04ef974055785","intervals":[[41,45],[157,157],[194,196],[288,290],[348,348],[354,354],[357,357],[377